#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:1
msgid "LinearFitResult"
msgstr "LinearFitResult"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:3
msgid ""
"The immutable result object returned by [`lin_fit`](lin-fit.md). Its "
"numerical fields describe one fit; its optional Matplotlib figure can still "
"be edited and saved."
msgstr ""
"The immutable result object returned by [`lin_fit`](lin-fit.md). Its "
"numerical fields describe one fit; its optional Matplotlib figure can still "
"be edited and saved."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:5
msgid "Public attributes"
msgstr "Public attributes"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "Attribute"
msgstr "Attribute"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "Meaning"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`slope`, `intercept`"
msgstr "`slope`, `intercept`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "The fitted slope and intercept."
msgstr "The fitted slope and intercept."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`slope_std`, `intercept_std`"
msgstr "`slope_std`, `intercept_std`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "Their standard uncertainties."
msgstr "Their standard uncertainties."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`covariance`"
msgstr "`covariance`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "Covariance between slope and intercept."
msgstr "Covariance between slope and intercept."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`correlation`"
msgstr "`correlation`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "Parameter correlation, or `None` when undefined."
msgstr "Parameter correlation, or `None` when undefined."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`residuals`"
msgstr "`residuals`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "Read-only physical residuals, `y - (slope*x + intercept)`."
msgstr "Read-only physical residuals, `y - (slope*x + intercept)`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`residual_std`"
msgstr "`residual_std`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid ""
"Square root of the residual sum of squares divided by `dof`, or `None` if "
"`dof=0`."
msgstr ""
"Square root of the residual sum of squares divided by `dof`, or `None` if "
"`dof=0`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`estimated_sigma`"
msgstr "`estimated_sigma`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid ""
"Common vertical dispersion estimated in OLS; equals `residual_std` in OLS "
"and is `None` in WLS."
msgstr ""
"Common vertical dispersion estimated in OLS; equals `residual_std` in OLS "
"and is `None` in WLS."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`chi2`"
msgstr "`chi2`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid ""
"Weighted residual criterion, or `None` in OLS. Iterative WLS uses effective "
"variances."
msgstr ""
"Weighted residual criterion, or `None` in OLS. Iterative WLS uses effective "
"variances."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`reduced_chi2`"
msgstr "`reduced_chi2`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`chi2 / dof`, or `None` when undefined."
msgstr "`chi2 / dof`, or `None` when undefined."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`p_value`"
msgstr "`p_value`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid ""
"Upper-tail chi-square probability, or `None` in OLS or with zero degrees of "
"freedom. Approximate in iterative WLS."
msgstr ""
"Upper-tail chi-square probability, or `None` in OLS or with zero degrees of "
"freedom. Approximate in iterative WLS."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`dof`"
msgstr "`dof`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "Number of observations minus two."
msgstr "Number of observations minus two."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`fit_method`"
msgstr "`fit_method`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`\"ols\"` or `\"wls\"`."
msgstr "`\"ols\"` or `\"wls\"`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`x_error_method`"
msgstr "`x_error_method`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`\"none\"` or `\"iterate\"`; a keyword-only field defaulting to `\"none\"`."
msgstr "`\"none\"` or `\"iterate\"`; a keyword-only field defaulting to `\"none\"`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "`figure`"
msgstr "`figure`"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md
msgid "Matplotlib figure, or `None` when `plot=False`."
msgstr "Matplotlib figure, or `None` when `plot=False`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:24
msgid ""
"For `x_error_method=\"iterate\"`, parameter covariance, the band, and the "
"interpretation of chi-squared and p-value belong to the historical "
"effective-variance approximation. They are not validated York/ODR results. "
"`fit_method` remains `\"wls\"` and `estimated_sigma` remains `None`."
msgstr ""
"For `x_error_method=\"iterate\"`, parameter covariance, the band, and the "
"interpretation of chi-squared and p-value belong to the historical "
"effective-variance approximation. They are not validated York/ODR results. "
"`fit_method` remains `\"wls\"` and `estimated_sigma` remains `None`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:26
msgid ""
"`normalize_residuals` changes only the plot; `residuals` always keep the "
"units of `y`. Changes to fitted fields through `dataclasses.replace()` are "
"rejected when they would disagree with the retained fit. You may modify "
"`result.figure` and save it separately; this does not update an earlier "
"automatic PDF export."
msgstr ""
"`normalize_residuals` changes only the plot; `residuals` always keep the "
"units of `y`. Changes to fitted fields through `dataclasses.replace()` are "
"rejected when they would disagree with the retained fit. You may modify "
"`result.figure` and save it separately; this does not update an earlier "
"automatic PDF export."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:28
msgid "Prediction"
msgstr "Prediction"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:35
msgid ""
"`predict()` accepts a finite real scalar or one-dimensional vector. It uses "
"the retained local representation to preserve accuracy near large coordinate"
" offsets."
msgstr ""
"`predict()` accepts a finite real scalar or one-dimensional vector. It uses "
"the retained local representation to preserve accuracy near large coordinate"
" offsets."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:37
msgid "TOML export"
msgstr "TOML export"

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:43
msgid ""
"The destination directory must already exist. A missing extension becomes "
"`.toml`; an existing destination is replaced atomically. The method returns "
"the written `Path`."
msgstr ""
"The destination directory must already exist. A missing extension becomes "
"`.toml`; an existing destination is replaced atomically. The method returns "
"the written `Path`."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:45
msgid ""
"The document contains `[mespy]`, `[fit]`, `[diagnostics]`, and "
"`[residuals]`, plus `[data]` and `[plot]` for results produced by `lin_fit`."
" Input uncertainties are stored in their original form after scalar "
"expansion, and floating-point results keep full precision. Undefined "
"diagnostics are omitted. Figure edits and the full Matplotlib configuration "
"are not serialized."
msgstr ""
"The document contains `[mespy]`, `[fit]`, `[diagnostics]`, and "
"`[residuals]`, plus `[data]` and `[plot]` for results produced by `lin_fit`."
" Input uncertainties are stored in their original form after scalar "
"expansion, and floating-point results keep full precision. Undefined "
"diagnostics are omitted. Figure edits and the full Matplotlib configuration "
"are not serialized."

#: ../../source/moduli/fit_utils/linear-fit-result.md:47
msgid ""
"Without `sigma_x`, exports retain schema 2. With `sigma_x`, schema 3 also "
"stores `[data].sigma_x` and `[fit].x_error_method`, including `\"none\"` "
"when horizontal bars were only displayed. Manually constructed iterative "
"results use schema 3 and record the method without inventing input data."
msgstr ""
"Without `sigma_x`, exports retain schema 2. With `sigma_x`, schema 3 also "
"stores `[data].sigma_x` and `[fit].x_error_method`, including `\"none\"` "
"when horizontal bars were only displayed. Manually constructed iterative "
"results use schema 3 and record the method without inventing input data."
